---
// About + privacy page.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="about/privacy — cultural/digital/insight"
  description="How this site was built, the fonts it uses, and how it handles your data."
>
  <main class="page">
    <h1>about/privacy</h1>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h-about">ABOUT THIS SITE</h2>
      <p>This site was built collaboratively in Claude Code, using Anthropic's
      Claude Fable 5 model — the pages, the cycling wordmark, and this sentence
      included. It's a static site built with Astro, hosted on Vercel, with the
      fonts self-hosted and no scripts beyond the analytics described below.</p>
      <p>The wordmark cycles through four open-source typefaces from Google
      Fonts: Silkscreen by Jason Kottke, Bitcount by Petr van Blokland,
      Atomic Age by Astigmatic, and Tourney by Tyler Finck. The headings around
      the site borrow the same four faces.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h-about">SEE ALSO</h2>
      <p>Adrian spent 25 years working in collections and digital at Te Papa, and
      after a restructure that included a significant deprioritisation of digital
      as a channel for sharing collections and research, he suddenly found himself
      with a lot of time on his hands. Consultancy is one way of filling that
      time, and maintaining some purpose in life, but he's also been building a
      few other things. Check out <a href="https://nextepisode.nz/">nextepisode.nz</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h-privacy">PRIVACY</h2>
      <p>This site uses Google Analytics to understand how it's used — pages
      viewed, rough location, and device type. That data is aggregated and
      anonymous; it isn't used for advertising and isn't shared.</p>
      <p>The site itself collects no personal information and sets no cookies of
      its own. If you email <a href="mailto:info@culturaldigitalinsight.nz">info@culturaldigitalinsight.nz</a>,
      your message is used only to reply to you.</p>
      <p>Questions about any of this are welcome at the same address.</p>
    </section>

    <nav>
      <a href="/">cultural/digital/insight</a>
    </nav>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 14vh 24px;
  }

  /* Each header takes one of the hero faces (links keep Silkscreen, so all
     four brand fonts appear on the page). */
  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 8vh;
    font-family: 'Tourney', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 6vw, 48px);
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 6vh 0 28px;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3.6vw, 30px);
    letter-spacing: 2px;
  }
  .h-about   { font-family: 'Bitcount Single', monospace; }
  .h-privacy { font-family: 'Atomic Age', serif; letter-spacing: 3px; }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* Body links sit inside prose — inherit its size rather than the
     site-wide Silkscreen link treatment. */
  p a {
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: inherit;
    line-height: inherit;
  }

  nav {
    margin-top: 10vh;
  }
</style>
